      common /circom/ acc, ver, rev, chat
@ Instead of using fragile [[block data]] subroutines, we use a magic
number to tag [[/circom/]] as initialized:
<<4-byte aligned part of [[/circom/]]>>=
      integer magic
      common /circom/ magic
@
<<[[parameter]] part of [[/circom/]]>>=
      integer MAGIC0
      parameter (MAGIC0 = 1904 06 16)
@ Since negative values are no updated, we can call [[circes]] with
all negative variables to ensure initialization:
<<Initialization check>>=
      if (magic .ne. MAGIC0) then
         call circes (-1d0, -1d0, -1d0, -1, -1, -1, -1)
      endif
@ 
